WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.000
Where to spend your hours.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.809
The failure mode with frontier topics is not ignorance.

3
00:00:05.809 --> 00:00:08.233
It is misallocating scarce study time.

4
00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:11.233
Here is the honest allocation.

5
00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:15.633
Spend your hours on the most valuable thing, not the most exciting one.

6
00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:20.300
Quantum is the most seductive item on the page, and deserves the least time.

7
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.633
Here is the split.

8
00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:26.440
Eighty four percent goes to your core skills and projects.

9
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.100
That is what gets hired, promoted, and paid.

10
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:37.096
Interpretability and evals get five percent, confidential computing and privacy three, and post quantum migration two.

11
00:00:37.096 --> 00:00:38.400
These are ready now.

12
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:44.333
Embodied AI gets three percent, quantum two, and neuromorphic or photonic just one.

13
00:00:45.533 --> 00:00:47.067
Why keep the frontier small?

14
00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:48.700
Picture two engineers.

15
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.891
One ships an evaluated RAG system and can also explain barren plateaus.

16
00:00:53.891 --> 00:00:55.200
That is impressive.

17
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.112
The other can only explain barren plateaus.

18
00:00:58.112 --> 00:00:59.267
That is a hobbyist.

19
00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.800
The WATCH items are the ones that will move.

20
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.300
So re-read the page every six months.

21
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:06.967
Check the watch items.

22
00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:10.433
When one flips to now, you already have the vocabulary.

23
00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:12.975
You move in weeks instead of months.

24
00:01:12.975 --> 00:01:16.400
The goal is not to be early, but to never be surprised.

25
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.067
The trap is spending your best hours on quantum because it feels like the future.

26
00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:27.467
Understand the mechanism once, keep it to about two percent, and keep shipping what pays.

27
00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:29.378
Let's recap.

28
00:01:29.378 --> 00:01:33.467
Eighty four percent of your time belongs to core skills and projects.

29
00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:37.667
Frontier literacy is a second layer on proven production ability.

30
00:01:37.967 --> 00:01:42.200
Interpretability, privacy, and post quantum beat quantum for time.

31
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.700
And re-read this page every six months.
